# p_9c4e — Marco's Work Kit: Seven Items Leave at 13:40

Every weekday, Marco's personal carry items — keys, wallet, shoes, notebook, water bottle, backpack, and phone — sit at the entry area (hook, floor, or table) from the pre-dawn hours until about 13:40, then vanish from the house entirely until he returns around 23:00. The robot sees them at the entry in the 00:00–12:00 passes and never again on weekdays. This is not a matter of the robot not looking; the items simply are not in the house. The phone disappears a bit earlier (last seen at 08:00 at the coffee table or nightstand), suggesting Marco picks it up when he starts his morning routine.

What sets this apart: p_a1b2 and p_b7c2 both claim that Marco's lunchbox, vitamins, or journal leave with him. The data refutes this: the lunchbox is at cupboard_k1 on all three sighted days (22 sightings, one receptacle), the vitamins at counter_k1 (3/3 days), and the journal at desk_b1 or nightstand_b1. Only the seven entry-area items travel. The scarf and umbrella stay at the entry (confirmed by p_f3e9 and the class:scarf / class:umbrella blocks that hold at 0.99–1.00).

Refutation: if the robot finds Marco's keys, wallet, shoes, or backpack anywhere in the house between 14:00 and 22:00 on a weekday, this document is wrong. If the lunchbox or vitamins are found OUT_OF_HOUSE during the work shift, the boundary between "work kit" and "stays home" is drawn wrong.

